      "votes": 0,
      "postDate": "2026-08-19T13:23:22.243000",
      "content": "<p>I had an alternative approach based on using Claude Fable to build game-specific solvers that solved 7 of the 25 public games and hit ~38% RHAE overall at 116/183 levels. That really worked, but it's utterly impractical here because it needed Claude access and it took 5 days to slog through the 25 games, not two hours and an RTX Pro 6000.</p>\n<p>The second approach was to build a general solver using what it learned from the previous effort. That got to 8 levels out of 183 but it kept overfitting so it has been discarded as well.</p>"
